				\begin{document}$$P(n) = [p_{1} (n), p_{2} (n),\, \ldots\!, p_{20} (n)]$$\end{document}P(n)=[p1(n),p2(n),…,p20(n)]

It is generally agreed that the DPC: Dipeptide composition describes the kinds and amounts of every conceivable pair of amino acids that can come after each other in a peptide. The number of potential dipeptides is 400, with each one containing two amino acids in a predetermined sequence [35, 36]. The following equation can be used to represent DPC:3\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
